Description:
    Generate a new validator with auto-generated UUID and boilerplate code.
    
    The generator will:
    - Automatically find the next validator number (e.g., v098, v099)
    - Generate a unique UUID for task_id
    - Create validator file with complete template
    - Include best practices and examples in comments

Example:
    rails generate validator book_premium_hotel "预订高档酒店" "用户需要预订五星级酒店，价格不限"

    This will create:
        app/validators/v098_book_premium_hotel_validator.rb

Arguments:
    validator_name (required):
        Snake case name for the validator
        Example: book_premium_hotel, search_flights, redeem_coupon
        
    title (required):
        Chinese title for the validator
        Example: "预订高档酒店", "搜索航班", "兑换优惠券"
        
    description (required):
        Chinese description of the task
        Example: "用户需要预订五星级酒店，价格不限"

After Generation:
    1. Open the generated file in app/validators/
    2. Implement the prepare method (set task parameters)
    3. Implement the verify method (add assertions with weights)
    4. Implement the simulate method (AI agent automation logic)
    5. Run: rake validator:simulate to test all validators

Best Practices:
    - Total assertion weights must sum to 100
    - First assertion should query records and store in @instance_variable
    - Use guard clause (return unless @record) after first assertion
    - Always filter by data_version in queries:
      * data_version: 0 for baseline data
      * data_version: @data_version for execution-specific data
    - Provide clear error messages in expect statements
    - Follow the query pattern shown in docs/project.md

Example Usage Flow:
    # Generate validator
    rails generate validator book_best_hotel "预订最佳酒店" "预订评分最高的经济型酒店"
    
    # Edit app/validators/v098_book_best_hotel_validator.rb
    # Implement prepare, verify, simulate methods
    
    # Test the validator
    rake validator:simulate
    
    # Check results
    # All validators should pass with 100/100 score
